<title>USA: Md. panel approves $1.5 mln for local companies.</title>
<headline>Md. panel approves $1.5 mln for local companies.</headline>
<dateline>ANNAPOLIS, Md. 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A committee of Maryland lawmakers has approved $1.5 million in aid to two Maryland businesses that is expected to create new 125 jobs.</p>
<p>The legislators agreed to a $1 million loan to the Bata Shoe Company in Belcamp. The loan will finance an expansion that will create more than 100 new jobs.</p>
<p>The committee also approved a half-million dollar loan to the Solo Cup Company in Havre De Grace. Solo plans to add another 25 jobs to the 500 existing positions in Harford County.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
